  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Chainlink is a decentralised oracle network that enables smart contracts on any blockchain to securely access off-chain data, computation, and cross-chain interoperability services. Founded by Sergey Nazarov and Steve Ellis, it operates a network of independent node operators that retrieve, aggregate, and deliver external data \u2014 price feeds, weather data, randomness, event outcomes \u2014 to on-chain smart contracts, bridging the oracle problem that prevents blockchains from natively accessing real-world information. Chainlink's native token (LINK) incentivises node operators and is staked as collateral to provide cryptoeconomic guarantees of data accuracy.",
